Entities

.special codes used to display reserved characters, symbols, or invisible spaces in a webpage that cannot be typed 
directly or have special meanings in HTML 
.used to display special characters that HTML normally reserves 
.always start with & and end with ;
.help avoid errors or misinterpretation in HTML code 
.commonly used for symbols, non-breaking spaces, and mathematical signs 
.make web content more readable and properly formatted 

list

Reserved characters
.either reserved for HTML or are not present in the basic keyboard & can't be used directly
        character                       entity name
        &                                  &amp;
        <                                  &lt;
        >                                  &gt;
        "                                  &quot;


Other characters
.aren't available directly on the keyboard therefore only the entity number can be used to represent it
    .keywords are not directly available to type, therefore need to specify their entity number 

Non-breaking space
.provides space that will not break into a new line
.the HTML entity is represented by &nbsp; that will separate the 2 words & will stick together without breaking it into a new line
.can also be used for preventing the browsers from truncating spaces in HTML pages 
.the non-breaking hyphen (-) is used to define a hyphen character that doesn't break into a new line

Combining diacritical marks 
.symbols added to a letter 
    .like the different accents 
.can be placed above, below, or inside a letter, or between two letters

Pointers
.use named entities when possible 
.verify entity codes 
.use entities for readability and compliance 